btBatchedConstraints: the spatial grid's cell a hair larger than the largest constraint extent

Jahshaka's change, BULLET-BATCHING-1 stage 1 (2026-10-19). A genuine upstream
defect: bulletphysics/bullet3 at the pinned 3.25 (2c204c49e), file
src/BulletDynamics/ConstraintSolver/btBatchedConstraints.cpp — unfixed on
upstream master as far as the pin's history shows; an upstream PR is owed (with
0002, the same grid's second rounding fault).

The bug
-------
setupSpatialGridBatchesMt (btBatchedConstraints.cpp:895) sets the grid's cell
size to EXACTLY the largest extent of any dynamic-dynamic constraint
(`btVector3 gridCellSize = consExtent;`, consExtent from
findMaxDynamicConstraintExtent :653-676), then puts each body in the cell
`int((p - bboxMin) * invGridCellSize)` (:945-955), invGridCellSize = 1 / size
rounded. Each factor of that product is rounded, so two bodies whose distance
on an axis equals the extent to the last ulp can land TWO cells apart.
assignConstraintsToGridBatches then breaks its premise
`btAssert(coordMax == coordMin + 1)` (:729):
  * Debug: an abort. Reproduced on the Jahshaka box with
    `test_physics_step_cost --bodies 500 --penetrating --island-batching`
    (a pile exploding apart; every position finite when it fires).
  * Release: the assert compiles away and the constraint is given a phase
    whose batches are assumed body-disjoint — two batches of one phase then
    share a body and are solved on two threads at once: a DATA RACE on the
    body's velocity.

The fix
-------
The cell is the extent times (1 + 1e-3). Two bodies at distance <= extent
then differ by at most 1/(1 + 1e-3) ~ 0.999 of a cell before rounding; the
rounding is a few ulps of a cell coordinate, and a coordinate is below ~257
cells (the grid is held to 128 chunks of 2x2x2 cells, :925-941), so about
1e-4 of a cell in single precision at the worst — the 1e-3 margin holds it
with an order of magnitude to spare. A cell 0.1 % larger changes the batch
count by nothing measurable. One line (plus its comment).

diff --git a/src/BulletDynamics/ConstraintSolver/btBatchedConstraints.cpp b/src/BulletDynamics/ConstraintSolver/btBatchedConstraints.cpp
index 89bd067a2..6dfa010f0 100644
--- a/src/BulletDynamics/ConstraintSolver/btBatchedConstraints.cpp
+++ b/src/BulletDynamics/ConstraintSolver/btBatchedConstraints.cpp
@@ -892,7 +892,12 @@ static void setupSpatialGridBatchesMt(
 
 	gridExtent.setMax(btVector3(btScalar(1), btScalar(1), btScalar(1)));
 
-	btVector3 gridCellSize = consExtent;
+	// The cell is a hair LARGER than the largest constraint extent (Jahshaka bullet-patches/0001): a body's cell is
+	// int((pos - bboxMin) * (1 / cellSize)), each factor rounded, so two bodies exactly one extent apart could land
+	// two cells apart and break the assert in assignConstraintsToGridBatches (coordMax == coordMin + 1) -- in Release
+	// two batches of one phase then share a body (a data race). 1e-3 of margin dwarfs the rounding (a few ulps of a
+	// coordinate under ~257 cells: about 1e-4 of a cell).
+	btVector3 gridCellSize = consExtent * btScalar(1 + 1e-3);
 	int gridDim[3];
 	gridDim[0] = int(1.0 + gridExtent.x() / gridCellSize.x());
 	gridDim[1] = int(1.0 + gridExtent.y() / gridCellSize.y());
